      "content": "It's definitely more descriptive now, but the auditor is still rejecting it. It's still way too low on the word count scale to be considered \"complete\" by the system. \n\nTry to really beef it up. You can probably add a \"Prerequisites\" section, an \"Introduction\" to what VortexScale is, and maybe a more detailed \"Troubleshooting\" or \"Verification\" section at the end to ensure everything worked. I still want it to be useful, but we really need a significant increase in the word count to get past this automated gatekeeper.",
